    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting favorable matchups against struggling arms, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**. **Kyle Tucker** earns our top score of 78.91, buoyed by a prime matchup against Kochanowicz, who provides an excellent 5.12 xERA environment. Similarly, **Andy Pages** sits at 69.36; while his score reflects a slight discount due to the catcher's arm and Kochanowicz\u2019s specific holding tendencies against the run, his spot in the batting order and the poor opposing SP skill make him a high-leverage start. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) rounds out our elite group, capitalizing on a strong wind-out factor in his park and a favorable matchup against Painter, giving him the highest score among our leadoff hitters today.\n\nConversely, we are exercising caution with several middle-tier options. **Gunnar Henderson** (63.31) remains a must-start despite a difficult matchup against Fisher, as his high-end sprint speed remains essential for our league-leading SB goals, and the potential for a \"slow delivery\" edge from the pitcher adds marginal value to his upside. The most difficult decision rested with **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 41.36 score. While he remains a depth piece, the lack of certainty regarding his batting order and his placement at the bottom of the lineup tipped the scale in favor of our more established starters. We are also monitoring **Dominic Smith** (42.40) closely; his proximity to our 40.0 \"Below Floor\" threshold makes him the most volatile asset in the lineup. All managers should note that **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Josh Jung** are currently operating on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions\u2014should these players drop in the order upon official posting, their efficiency scores will need immediate re-evaluation to ensure we aren't burning game caps on suboptimal slots.",
